	int "Minimum milliseconds between host-event flash persists"
	depends on TOTEM_HOST_EVENT_LOG
	default 60000
	range 5000 600000
	help
	  Coalesce settings writes during dual-host thrash. RAM ring still
	  records every event; only NVS is throttled. Dump still requests a
	  persist (subject to this interval).

config TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE
	bool "Pause advertising after the selected host has been away for a while"
	depends on ZMK_BLE
	default n
	help
	  When the selected profile's device has been disconnected for
	  TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE_TIMEOUT_MIN minutes, stop advertising to save power. A key
	  press on either half resumes it (the first press or two may be lost). This also
	  stops cross-talk -- nothing can connect while not advertising -- so it does not
	  need address-based filtering. Implemented by patches/zmk-ble.patch on our ZMK
	  fork. Central-only.

config TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE_TIMEOUT_MIN
	int "Minutes the selected host may be away before advertising is paused"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE
	default 5

config TOTEM_ADV_BOOST
	bool "Faster advertising after profile switch (and wake from dark)"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE
	default y
	help
	  For TOTEM_ADV_BOOST_SEC after a profile switch (or keypress resume from
	  advertising-dark), advertise at Bluetooth GAP "fast interval 1" (30-60 ms)
	  instead of ZMK's default "fast interval 2" (100-150 ms). Denser advertising
	  helps the newly selected host discover the keyboard sooner. Implemented in
	  patches/zmk-ble.patch. Central-only. Small extra radio use only during the
	  short boost window.

config TOTEM_ADV_BOOST_SEC
	int "Seconds of dense advertising after profile switch"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_BOOST
	default 12
	range 3 60

config TOTEM_ADV_POST_SWITCH_DARK
	bool "After profile-switch boost, go dark if selected host not connected"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_BOOST
	default y
	help
	  When the boost window after BT_SEL ends and the selected host is still
	  not connected, pause advertising until a keypress. Limits open-ad thrash
	  from background bonded hosts (which can rot the selected bond) without
	  Filter Accept List. Cost: if the host is slow, press any key to resume
	  advertising. Implemented in patches/zmk-ble.patch. Central-only.

config TOTEM_DIR_THEN_OPEN
	bool "Directed advertising then open undirected after profile switch"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE
	default n
	help
	  After BT_SEL (exclusive-host still drops the previous host), first
	  advertise *directed* to the active bonded peer for TOTEM_DIR_ADV_SEC,
	  then fall back to open undirected (with boost if enabled). Goal: faster
	  discovery for the selected host without multi-link. Directed may fail
	  on some privacy centrals — fail-open to undirected immediately.
	  Implemented in patches/zmk-ble.patch. Central-only.

config TOTEM_DIR_ADV_SEC
	int "Seconds of directed advertising after profile switch"
	depends on TOTEM_DIR_THEN_OPEN
	default 4
	range 1 15
	help
	  Low-duty directed phase length before open undirected. Keep short so
	  macOS (RPA) still gets undirected boost quickly if directed does not
	  help.

config TOTEM_IDLE_DISCONNECT
	bool "Disconnect the active host after a long keypress-idle window (then go dark)"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE
	default n
	help
	  On the central half: after CONFIG_TOTEM_IDLE_DISCONNECT_MIN minutes with no
	  keypress, disconnect the active host AND immediately pause advertising ("go
	  dark"), so it cannot instantly reconnect and wake the host. A key press resumes
	  advertising (via the throttle listener) and the host reconnects; an asleep/away
	  host simply stays gone, so idle drain falls to the throttled rate with no wake
	  storm. macOS keeps its BLE link alive during sleep, so without this the keyboard
	  stays connected-idle overnight. Requires TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE (shares its
	  advertising-pause machinery). Implemented in patches/zmk-ble.patch on the ZMK
	  fork, not a standalone module. Central-only.

config TOTEM_IDLE_DISCONNECT_MIN
	int "Minutes without a keypress before the active host is disconnected"
	depends on TOTEM_IDLE_DISCONNECT
	default 20

config TOTEM_RPA_DISCONNECT
	bool "Find RPA-connected hosts when disconnecting a profile"
	depends on ZMK_BLE
	default y
	help
	  zmk_ble_prof_disconnect() looks the host up only by its stored *identity*
	  address, which misses when the host is connected under a resolvable private
	  address (macOS always is) and returns -ENODEV. Meanwhile
	  zmk_ble_profile_is_connected() does resolve RPAs, so a stale conn object can
	  look connected while nothing is able to tear it down: update_advertising()
	  then stays dark on purpose, every recovery path skips, and repeated BT_SEL
	  does nothing -- only a power cycle recovers (observed 2026-07-24, macOS away
	  6 h). With this on, the disconnect falls back to the same IRK-aware conn
	  lookup. Side effect: BT_SEL on the already-active profile now really drops a
	  live macOS link instead of silently failing. Set n to restore the old
	  identity-address-only behaviour. Implemented in patches/zmk-ble.patch.

config TOTEM_ADV_RECONCILE
	bool "Rebuild advertising state from scratch on explicit user intent"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_THROTTLE
	default y
	help
	  A keypress while the selected host is down, or BT_SEL, means the user wants
	  that host connected now. Instead of trusting advertising_status (which can
	  claim ZMK_ADV_CONN while the controller is not advertising, a state
	  update_advertising() cannot leave because desired == current matches no
	  switch case), force the baseline: cancel throttle/retry work, clear the
	  throttle, stop advertising accepting -EALREADY, reset the status, restart.
	  Rate-limited by TOTEM_ADV_RECONCILE_COOLDOWN_MS so held or repeated keys
	  cannot thrash the radio. Never disconnects a host on a keypress -- only the
	  BT_SEL path may do that. Implemented in patches/zmk-ble.patch. Central-only.

config TOTEM_ADV_RECONCILE_COOLDOWN_MS
	int "Minimum milliseconds between keypress-driven advertising reconciles"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_RECONCILE
	default 10000
	range 1000 60000
	help
	  A reconcile restarts advertising, so doing it on every keystroke while the
	  host is away would keep resetting the advertising interval and make the
	  keyboard *harder* to discover. 10 s is well inside the couple of seconds a
	  present host needs to connect once ads are actually running.

config TOTEM_ZOMBIE_VERIFY_MS
	int "Milliseconds to confirm a BT_SEL disconnect actually tore the link down"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_RECONCILE
	default 2000
	range 500 10000
	help
	  After BT_SEL asks the active host to disconnect, re-check whether the
	  profile still reports connected. Still connected after this long means the
	  conn object is wedged -- objective evidence for TOTEM_RECOVERY_REBOOT.

config TOTEM_RECOVERY_REBOOT
	bool "Reboot the central as last resort when BLE recovery cannot proceed"
	depends on TOTEM_ADV_RECONCILE
	select REBOOT
	default y
	help
	  So the keyboard never needs its physical power switches to recover. Fires
	  only on objective evidence, never merely because a host is absent: either
	  bt_le_adv_start() returned genuine errors for the whole open-adv retry
	  budget after the user asked for a reconnect, or the active profile still
	  reported connected TOTEM_ZOMBIE_VERIFY_MS after a BT_SEL disconnect. Cold
	  reboot only -- equivalent to &sys_reset, so bonds, profiles and settings in
	  NVS all survive; this is NOT a settings reset. The peripheral half
	  reconnects on its own. Implemented in patches/zmk-ble.patch. Central-only.

config TOTEM_RECOVERY_REBOOT_MIN_UPTIME_SEC
	int "Seconds after boot during which no automatic recovery reboot may fire"
	depends on TOTEM_RECOVERY_REBOOT
	default 60
	range 10 600
	help
	  Loop breaker: recovery state does not survive a reboot, so without an
	  uptime floor a permanently broken controller could reboot, be asked to
	  recover again, and reboot forever. Below this uptime the reboot is
	  suppressed and only logged.
